# Card kinds

A `kind` selects the spec schema a card carries. The envelope is always the same;
the kind changes the payload, not the ontology. The v1 doctrine defines 15
registrable kinds. `External` is a discriminator for foreign schema
descriptors, not a sixteenth kind you can register.

<Aside title="What runs end-to-end" data-variant="wyrd">

**Data**, **Model**, and **Prompt** are shipped: authored in Python, validated,
saved, and — for Prompt — resolved by the Skald runtime. The verification kinds
are also shipped: a **Verifier** with a `drift` or `eval` implementation is
attached to a subject through a `verified_by` binding, a **Trigger** decides
when the server runs it, and **Operators** react when a run fails. The other
kinds have an authored spec and JSON Schema but no runtime behind them yet. The
tables below mark each one. See [Cards](/cards/) for per-field reference on the
shipped kinds.

</Aside>

